// The `expected_hash` field is `"blake3:" + lowercase-hex(blake3-digest)`.
//
// Differs from the sibling `0xdeadbeefdeadbeef.ron` 60-tick smoke pin
// in three ways that broaden cross-OS determinism coverage:
//
//   1. Tick count: 600 vs 60 — long-horizon coverage exercises ball
//      physics through multiple KickOff cycles + signature cooldown
//      windows that fire/expire/refire over the run.
//   2. Init constructor: `MatchState::initial_with_content(seed, &content)`
//      vs bare `MatchState::initial(seed)` — slot 7's
//      `signature_candidates` is populated from the first AM
//      `PlayerTemplate` in the loaded `ContentStore`.
//   3. Signature definitions: `&content.signature_definitions` passed to
//      every `tick_match` call vs the empty `&BTreeMap::new()` the smoke
//      pin uses — so the signature dispatcher actually fires across the
//      600 ticks instead of being a no-op.
//
// Re-baseline cadence: same as the smoke pin. Any canonical-state schema
// bump (new field on MatchState / BallState / PlayerState / MatchEvent)
// drifts this hash; re-pin alongside the existing 60-tick pin via the
// rebase procedure at `docs/specs/determinism-gate.md` §9.
//
// Re-baseline history:
//   2026-05-16 (T1-8) — initial pin `66585ca8…4625` on the content-loaded
